index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d91bcdda69fbd9576eb2b39995c4f12767ba4f9c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/archive/2026-11-17-add-booking-cancellation/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+## Context
+
+`createRentalService()` keeps bookings in an array of `Booking & { from, to }`; `isFree` scans it, and both
+`book` and `availability` rely on `isFree`. The cancellation policy (24 hours, full or nothing) is already
+recorded in the rentals spec.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Add `cancel(bookingId: string, at: string): Cancellation` to `RentalService`, with
+  `Cancellation { bookingId: string; refund: number }`.
+- Cancelling removes the booking from the array, so `isFree` needs no change and both `book` and
+  `availability` see the equipment as free. A separate `Set` of cancelled ids lets a second `cancel` be told
+  apart from an unknown id; both throw.
+- Parse `at` with a strict ISO-8601 UTC check (`Z` suffix, valid calendar date, like the existing parsers but
+  with any time of day) and validate it before mutating anything, so a failed call leaves the booking intact.
+- Refund is `booking.total` when `booking.from - at >= 24h`, otherwise 0. The start used is the booking's
+  own start instant, so day and hourly bookings share one rule.
+
+## Risks
+
+None significant: bookings that are never cancelled behave as before.
