@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Plans change and customers ask the desk to cancel their rentals. Today a booking can never be undone, so the
+equipment stays blocked and the desk cannot tell the customer what they get back.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `cancel(bookingId, at)` to the rental service. It cancels the booking at the instant `at` and returns
+  `{ bookingId, refund }`, the amount in euro cents given back to the customer.
+- The refund follows the cancellation policy already recorded in the rentals spec: nothing when `at` is less
+  than 24 hours before the booking start (including after the start), the full booking total otherwise.
+- A cancelled booking no longer holds its equipment: `book` and `availability` treat the period as free again.
+- A booking can only be cancelled once; an unknown booking id, a second cancellation or an invalid `at` throws.
+
+Scope: cancelling rentals of boards and sails at the booking desk.
+Out of scope: partial refunds, cancellation fees, lessons, customers, persistence, listing cancelled
+bookings, season (April to October) enforcement.
+
+No runtime dependency is introduced.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `rentals`: adds cancellation of bookings and replaces the "policy recorded for later" requirement.
+
+## Impact
+
+`src/index.ts` (new method and result type on `RentalService`) and `test/rental.test.ts`. Existing behavior
+is unchanged for bookings that are not cancelled.
